WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.633 --> 00:00:04.604
[music playing]

00:00:17.350 --> 00:00:19.219
We're headed to a warehouse.

00:00:19.285 --> 00:00:20.987
This one has a lot of
European shipments,

00:00:21.054 --> 00:00:24.023
South American shipments, a
lot of source countries for us

00:00:24.090 --> 00:00:25.692
for narcotics.

00:00:25.759 --> 00:00:27.694
So we're gonna see what
we can find over here.

00:00:27.761 --> 00:00:32.465
[music playing]

00:00:33.900 --> 00:00:35.068
Albert, take a look at this.

00:00:35.135 --> 00:00:36.069
Ecuador.

00:00:36.136 --> 00:00:36.970
What is that?

00:00:37.036 --> 00:00:37.804
I don't know.

00:00:37.871 --> 00:00:40.006
Let's find out.

00:00:40.073 --> 00:00:41.174
It's, like, blankets.

00:00:43.610 --> 00:00:45.545
Ecuador is a big
transit point now for dope

00:00:45.612 --> 00:00:47.380
coming out from South America.

00:00:47.447 --> 00:00:50.049
Heroin, cocaine, we used to
get stuff in the embroidery

00:00:50.116 --> 00:00:52.585
of this, inside the lining.

00:00:52.652 --> 00:00:55.722
A lot of times, what they
try to do is nickel and dime.

00:00:55.789 --> 00:00:57.390
So they'll put little
baggies of coke

00:00:57.457 --> 00:00:58.825
inside of little handicrafts.

00:00:58.892 --> 00:00:59.726
You always got to check.

00:00:59.793 --> 00:01:00.960
You gotta cut it open.

00:01:01.027 --> 00:01:02.262
This one is what it is.

00:01:02.328 --> 00:01:03.763
OFFICER RAMIREZ: All
right, I've seen enough.

00:01:03.830 --> 00:01:04.597
Yeah.

00:01:04.664 --> 00:01:08.401
[music playing]

00:01:11.171 --> 00:01:12.906
Coming from Mexico.

00:01:12.972 --> 00:01:13.873
Yeah.

00:01:13.940 --> 00:01:15.408
It's all food and breads.

00:01:15.475 --> 00:01:17.977
OFFICER TWAROWSKI: In
here, you got peanuts.

00:01:18.044 --> 00:01:19.412
Tamales.

00:01:19.479 --> 00:01:21.481
Looks like a lot of
shipments coming from Mexico.

00:01:21.548 --> 00:01:23.216
Mexico, a big source country.

00:01:23.283 --> 00:01:25.018
Cocaine, heroin,
fentanyl, every--

00:01:25.084 --> 00:01:26.052
Meth.

00:01:26.119 --> 00:01:27.454
--you know, meth, everything.

00:01:27.520 --> 00:01:29.222
So what they like to do
is they like to conceal it

00:01:29.289 --> 00:01:32.292
inside the food a lot of times.

00:01:32.358 --> 00:01:34.427
They think it's going
to fool the x-rays.

00:01:34.494 --> 00:01:36.062
Or they think it's going
to fool us, you know.

00:01:36.129 --> 00:01:37.297
We're not going to
take a look at it.

00:01:37.363 --> 00:01:40.900
But we take a look
at everything.

00:01:40.967 --> 00:01:41.734
You know, we have to.

00:01:47.774 --> 00:01:48.808
Those are Chilean apples.

00:01:48.875 --> 00:01:49.776
Those are bigger.

00:01:49.843 --> 00:01:51.911
So it's a different fruit.

00:01:51.978 --> 00:01:52.779
OFFICER RAMIREZ: Nothing.

00:01:52.846 --> 00:01:54.180
Not as sticky.

00:01:54.247 --> 00:01:55.515
ASSISTANT PORT
DIRECTOR GALANTINO:

00:01:55.582 --> 00:01:57.150
It's funny that those
were a different color.

00:01:57.217 --> 00:02:01.454
[music playing]

00:02:08.928 --> 00:02:10.330
There's another one.

00:02:10.396 --> 00:02:13.366
Now, we're separating
the actual contraband

00:02:13.433 --> 00:02:15.635
itself from the fruit.

00:02:15.702 --> 00:02:18.605
I wish they'd chosen
something that was less syrupy.

00:02:18.671 --> 00:02:21.641
They think we're not going
to get our hands dirty.

00:02:21.708 --> 00:02:23.543
So what do you got there?
OFFICER TWAROWSKI: Five, seven.

00:02:23.610 --> 00:02:25.178
ASSISTANT PORT DIRECTOR
GALANTINO: This one has--

00:02:25.245 --> 00:02:26.179
yep, seven.

00:02:28.448 --> 00:02:30.250
What we do now, we're
going to use our Gemini

00:02:30.316 --> 00:02:32.218
machine to just confirm.

00:02:32.285 --> 00:02:36.656
[music playing]

00:02:37.724 --> 00:02:40.360
There you go.

00:02:40.426 --> 00:02:43.062
It's cocaine hydrochloride.

00:02:43.129 --> 00:02:45.465
OFFICER RAMIREZ: Get
a weight on this.

00:02:45.532 --> 00:02:47.066
OFFICER TWAROWSKI: All right.

00:02:47.133 --> 00:02:51.671
[music playing]

00:02:51.738 --> 00:02:55.842
0.391 kilograms.

00:02:55.909 --> 00:02:57.844
ASSISTANT PORT DIRECTOR
GALANTINO: I mean, they were

00:02:57.911 --> 00:02:59.312
not greedy, not greedy at all.

00:02:59.379 --> 00:03:00.914
OFFICER RAMIREZ: Not at all.

00:03:00.980 --> 00:03:04.150
And we have to dig through all
this food to get a small load.

00:03:04.217 --> 00:03:05.718
And this, we've been
seeing more and more,

00:03:05.785 --> 00:03:07.120
the smaller amounts.

00:03:07.186 --> 00:03:09.188
I think they're testing
out different concealments

00:03:09.255 --> 00:03:10.590
and seeing what they
can get through.

00:03:10.657 --> 00:03:13.226
They don't want to
lose a big shipment.

00:03:13.293 --> 00:03:15.128
Now, we're going
to notify HSI.

00:03:15.194 --> 00:03:17.263
And they're ultimately
going to take possession

00:03:17.330 --> 00:03:18.631
of the narcotics themselves.

00:03:18.698 --> 00:03:21.367
And they may do a
controlled delivery to find

00:03:21.434 --> 00:03:22.735
out who this was going to.

00:03:22.802 --> 00:03:24.070
OFFICER TWAROWSKI: Right.

00:03:24.137 --> 00:03:26.406
And then perhaps
develop a case from this.

00:03:26.472 --> 00:03:29.876
At the end of the day, it's
about disbanding these drug

00:03:29.943 --> 00:03:31.511
trafficking organizations.

00:03:31.578 --> 00:03:35.515
This shipment here, this is
just one of those 300 or 400

00:03:35.582 --> 00:03:39.285
that come in
multiple times a day.

00:03:39.352 --> 00:03:40.353
See what else they got.

